<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P51687">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_a753fd4037c9665a8035413300849d5b" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_521a64df0721b55c0cdca29336768cf0" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_19c8979034c6aa5b5f7304ed262ea679" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Sulfite oxidase, mitochondrial</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_SUOX_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P51687" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SUOX_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.8.3.1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SUOX</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference80721</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SUOX_HUMAN Reviewed; 545 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_rcsb_pdb_1MJ4_see-also</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_6821</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=H2O + O2 + sulfite = H2O2 + sulfate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:24600, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15379,ChEBI:CHEBI:16189, ChEBI:CHEBI:16240, ChEBI:CHEBI:17359;EC=1.8.3.1;COFACTOR:Name=heme b; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:60344;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12832761};Note=Binds 1 heme b (iron(II)-protoporphyrin IX) group non-covalently per subunit. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12832761};COFACTOR:Name=Mo-molybdopterin; Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:71302;Evidence={ECO:0000250};Note=Binds 1 Mo-molybdopterin (Mo-MPT) cofactor per subunit.{ECO:0000250};PATHWAY: Energy metabolism; sulfur metabolism.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000250}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Mitochondrion intermembrane space.DISEASE: Sulfite oxidase deficiency, isolated (ISOD) [MIM:272300]:A life-threatening, autosomal recessive neurometabolic disordercharacterized by severe neurological impairment. Classic ISODmanifests in the first few hours to days of life and ischaracterized by intractable seizures, feeding difficulties,rapidly progressive encephalopathy, microcephaly, and profoundintellectual disability. Children usually die during the first fewmonths of life. Mild ISOD manifests in infancy or early childhoodand is characterized by ectopia lentis that is variably present,developmental delay and regression, movement disordercharacterized by dystonia and choreoathetosis, ataxia, and rarelyacute hemiplegia due to metabolic stroke.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10519592, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12112661,ECO:0000269|PubMed:12368985, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9428520,ECO:0000269|PubMed:9600976}. Note=The disease is caused bymutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAA74886.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally extended.; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=AAL08048.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Note=Translation N-terminally extended.; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P51687_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_005269169</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

